# --- @fill: shop prepositions (beim / an der / op dem / am) -----------------
# The deck teaches where you shop with contracted dative prepositions.
# Distractors are sibling shop-prepositions — the confusion is which
# shop takes which form (person → bei, enclosed → an, open → op).

@fill
@lu Hie keeft Rëndsfleesch [beim] Metzler.
@en He buys beef [at the] butcher's.
@distractor-lu an der
@distractor-lu op dem
@distractor-lu am
@distractor-en in the
@distractor-en on the
@distractor-en from the

@fill
@lu Ech kafe mäi Brout [an der] Bäckerei.
@en I buy my bread [at the] bakery.
@distractor-lu beim
@distractor-lu op dem
@distractor-lu am
@distractor-en in the
@distractor-en on the
@distractor-en from the

@fill
@lu Hatt keeft Zalot [op dem] Maart.
@en She buys salad [at the] market.
@distractor-lu beim
@distractor-lu an der
@distractor-lu am
@distractor-en in the
@distractor-en from the
@distractor-en by the

@fill
@lu Mir kafe Mëllech [am] Supermarché.
@en We buy milk [at the] supermarket.
@distractor-lu beim
@distractor-lu an der
@distractor-lu op dem
@distractor-en in the
@distractor-en on the
@distractor-en from the

# --- @fill: mäi vs meng possessives ------------------------------------------
# mäi + m/n singular, meng + f singular and all plurals. Distractors
# are the other possessive form and deng/seng for a three-way contrast.

@fill
@lu Ech kafe [mäi] Kéis um Maart.
@en I buy [my] cheese at the market.
@distractor-lu meng
@distractor-lu deng
@distractor-lu seng
@distractor-en your
@distractor-en his
@distractor-en her

@fill
@lu Ech kafe [meng] Zeitung bei dem Bäcker.
@en I buy [my] newspaper at the baker's.
@distractor-lu mäi
@distractor-lu deng
@distractor-lu seng
@distractor-en your
@distractor-en his
@distractor-en her

@fill
@lu Wou ass [mäi] Brout?
@en Where is [my] bread?
@distractor-lu meng
@distractor-lu deng
@distractor-lu seng
@distractor-en your
@distractor-en his
@distractor-en her

# --- @fill: kascht vs kaschten -----------------------------------------------
# Singular kascht vs. plural kaschten — the price-question verb agreement.
# Distractors are the wrong number form plus kritt/hëlt.

@fill
@lu Dat Brout [kascht] dräi Euro.
@en That bread [costs] three euros.
@distractor-lu kaschten
@distractor-lu kritt
@distractor-lu hëlt
@distractor-en cost
@distractor-en gets
@distractor-en takes

@fill
@lu Déi Drauwe [kaschten] véier Euro.
@en Those grapes [cost] four euros.
@distractor-lu kascht
@distractor-lu kritt
@distractor-lu hëlt
@distractor-en costs
@distractor-en gets
@distractor-en takes

# --- @fill: payment method (boer vs mat der Kaart) ---------------------------
