# --- @fill: copula sinn vs ass -----------------------------------------------
# Plural subjects take sinn, singular takes ass — the quality questions
# the deck drills. Distractors are the wrong number form.

@fill
@lu [Sinn] d'Drauwe frësch?
@en [Are] the grapes fresh?
@distractor-lu Ass
@distractor-lu Huet
@distractor-lu Gëtt
@distractor-en Is
@distractor-en Has
@distractor-en Does

@fill
@lu [Ass] de Sak Grompere schwéier?
@en [Is] the sack of potatoes heavy?
@distractor-lu Sinn
@distractor-lu Huet
@distractor-lu Gëtt
@distractor-en Are
@distractor-en Has
@distractor-en Does

# --- @fill: ordering patterns (hätt gär / huelen / gitt mir) ----------------
# The deck teaches four client ordering frames. Distractors are the
# other ordering verbs — the confusion is which polite frame to use.

@fill
@lu Ech [hätt gär] e Kilo Tomaten, wgl.
@en I [would like] a kilo of tomatoes, please.
@distractor-lu kréie gär
@distractor-lu brauche just
@distractor-lu siche nach
@distractor-en want to get
@distractor-en just need
@distractor-en am looking for

@fill
@lu [Gitt] mir dräi Orangë, wgl.!
@en [Give] me three oranges, please!
@distractor-lu Schéckt
@distractor-lu Bréngt
@distractor-lu Weist
@distractor-en Send
@distractor-en Bring
@distractor-en Show

@fill
@lu Ech [huelen] och e Pak Miel, wgl.
@en I'll [take] also a pack of flour, please.
@distractor-lu kréien
@distractor-lu brauchen
@distractor-lu sichen
@distractor-en get
@distractor-en need
@distractor-en find

# --- @fill: oder vs an connectors --------------------------------------------
# The quality questions and shopping lists use oder (or) vs an (and).
# Distractors are sibling connectors — mee (but), well (because).

@fill
@lu Sinn d'Äppel séiss [oder] sauer?
@en Are the apples sweet [or] sour?
@distractor-lu an
@distractor-lu mee
@distractor-lu well
@distractor-en and
@distractor-en but
@distractor-en because

@fill
@lu Si keeft Brout, e Kuch [an] eng Taart.
@en She buys bread, a cake [and] a tart.
@distractor-lu oder
@distractor-lu mee
@distractor-lu well
@distractor-en or
@distractor-en but
@distractor-en because
